      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name}: If a URL loads a site that is not immediately seen as a video/stream, I would definitely expect the InvalidURL error to occur, as it is a URL loading-related error. I'm not sure how PlayerError is also caused in this situation, though the vagueness of what PlayerError is also contributes to my confusion. If there are remote edge cases where multiple errors can be sent by a video player, than video player systems that act based on certain errors are surely going to have issues with these repeated calls. As well, the error reporting is not instant. The second error happens about 1 second later, so it is unclear if the errors are happening at the same time and reporting is buffered, or the video player is still attempting to work with the known InvalidURL error and then hitting the PlayerError as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-06T23:10:46.594Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Attempting to load, for example, \"https://www.youtube.com/\" in a video player, both AVPro and Unity, will cause OnVideoError to fire twice. The first one will be for InvalidURL, while the second is PlayerError.\nhttps://vrch.at/focky-scruffysteve-4d3ef",
